<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Checkboxes, and the third state</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      Checking a branch checks its subtree; checking some of its children leaves the branch
      <em>mixed</em>. That third state is the reason a tree is not a list with indents — and it
      is computed from the subtree, never stored, so it cannot go stale.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-stack">
      <pdx-tree label="Permissions" checkable default-expand-all :nodes="permissions"></pdx-tree>
    </div>
  </section>
</template>

